      en: ["The Genko Borui sea wall was built between 1274 and 1281.", "The wall stretches about 20 kilometers along the coast of Hakata Bay.", "It is constructed mainly from local basalt and mortared stones.", "The average height of the wall is 2–3 meters.", "After the first Mongol invasion in 1274, the fortification was strengthened.", "The second Mongol invasion in 1281 was stopped by a typhoon (kamikaze) and the wall."],
