      en: "Ouchijuku in Fukushima Prefecture is a former post town on the Aizu-Nishi-Kaido road from the Edo period. Founded in the 17th century, it served as a resting place for travelers and merchants. The street is lined with traditional thatched-roof houses, now used as shops, restaurants, and museums. Ouchijuku is part of the Tanohara area and is designated as an Important Preservation District for Groups of Traditional Buildings. The landscape with rice fields and mountains provides a scenic backdrop.",
