      en: "Sanjusangen-do in Kyoto is a Buddhist temple built in 1164 by Taira no Kiyomori. The name means 'Hall with 33 Spaces', referring to the number of bays between pillars. The hall is famous for its 1001 life-sized statues of Kannon, the goddess of mercy. The central statue is over 3 meters tall. The temple is a National Treasure of Japan.",
